::Software Development Life Cycle::
Which is NOT a benefit of prototyping?{
~Demonstrates a basic idea of how the final product works.
=Does not need any additional time or resources.
~Provides a "hands-on" design to be shown to stakeholders.
~Less expensive to change design/code with a prototype than the final product.
}

::Software Development Life Cycle::
which is NOT a way that the Software Development Life Cycle adds value to software development?{
~It helps in effectively planning before starting the actual development.
~It helps in reducing unnecessary costs during development.
~It enables developers to design and build high-quality software products. 
=It is a rigid framework that does not allow for deviation from any steps.
}
